OTSEC patch for HR-25, option A with option (a): frame-by-frame recovery in
Zeek 9.0.1's DNP3 analyzer, on top of HR-23's option (i)
(docs/phase4/D4-hr25-design.md; D1's ruling 6893095629, D4-106; option (a),
D4-112 item 3; D1's rulings on #782, D4-123). This file carries parts
HR25-B1 and HR25-B2 of the build (D4-124): sections 2.1 to 2.6 and 2.9 of
the design, the transport sequence check of section 2.3, the fourteen
causes counted (B1); confirmation at the first whole fragment, the budget
before it, the weirds gated, and the events dnp3_resync (why "first",
"interval", "end" and "budget") and dnp3_resync_mark (sections 2.7 and 2.8,
B2). The script part is zeek-patch/resync.zeek, which declares
DNP3::resync_report_interval.

Against: Zeek 9.0.1 (zeek-9.0.1.tar.gz, SHA-256 in build.env) with
hr23-fc-dispatch.patch applied. Applied after it, from the top of the
unpacked tree, with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0`.

The three files changed are Zeek 9.0.1's, under the BSD-3-Clause licence in
Zeek 9.0.1's COPYING, copied verbatim beside this patch as COPYING. The
lines this patch adds are the project's own (LICENSE.md). No grant to offer
them upstream exists, and any report to Zeek's maintainers waits for the
owner's word (design section 4, C5).


